[
    {
        "step_title": "SynoCli WiFi Tools",
        "items": [
            {
                "desc": "The tools to connect the NAS to a WiFi network, with the adapters of <b>synokernel-wifi</b>: load the driver of the adapter with <b>synocli-kernelmodule</b>, then connect with <b>wifi-connect</b> and the profile of the network:<br><br><code>synocli-kernelmodule list</code><br><code>sudo -i synocli-kernelmodule --profile rtl88x2bu start</code><br><code>sudo -i wifi-connect MyNetwork</code><br><br>To write the profile of a WiFi network:<br><code>sudo -i wifi-connect --new</code><br><br>Other options:<br><code>sudo -i wifi-connect --list</code> the profiles<br><code>sudo -i wifi-connect --status</code> the state of the connection<br><code>sudo -i wifi-connect --stop</code> disconnect<br><br>See the <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://docs.synocommunity.com/packages/synocli-wifi-tools/\">package documentation</a>."
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "step_title": "WiFi network",
        "items": [
            {
                "desc": "Optional: the profile of a network to connect to, in <code>/var/packages/synocli-wifi-tools/var/networks</code>, named after it. Leave the network empty to skip. The passphrase is kept as its WPA2 key, not in clear, except for WPA3, which needs it."
            },
            {
                "type": "textfield",
                "subitems": [
                    {
                        "key": "wizard_wifi_ssid",
                        "desc": "Network (SSID)",
                        "defaultValue": "",
                        "validator": {
                            "allowBlank": true
                        }
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "type": "password",
                "subitems": [
                    {
                        "key": "wizard_wifi_passphrase",
                        "desc": "Passphrase",
                        "defaultValue": "",
                        "validator": {
                            "allowBlank": true,
                            "minLength": 8,
                            "maxLength": 63
                        }
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "type": "singleselect",
                "desc": "<b>Security</b>",
                "subitems": [
                    {
                        "key": "wizard_wifi_wpa2",
                        "desc": "WPA2",
                        "defaultValue": true
                    },
                    {
                        "key": "wizard_wifi_wpa3",
                        "desc": "WPA3, or WPA2/WPA3",
                        "defaultValue": false
                    },
                    {
                        "key": "wizard_wifi_open",
                        "desc": "Open, no passphrase",
                        "defaultValue": false
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "type": "textfield",
                "subitems": [
                    {
                        "key": "wizard_wifi_country",
                        "desc": "Country, two letters as CA or FR, for the 5 GHz channels",
                        "defaultValue": "",
                        "validator": {
                            "allowBlank": true,
                            "regex": {
                                "expr": "/^[A-Za-z]{2}$/",
                                "errorText": "Two letters, as CA or FR"
                            }
                        }
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "type": "singleselect",
                "desc": "<b>Address</b>",
                "subitems": [
                    {
                        "key": "wizard_wifi_dhcp",
                        "desc": "By DHCP",
                        "defaultValue": true
                    },
                    {
                        "key": "wizard_wifi_static",
                        "desc": "Static, below",
                        "defaultValue": false
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "desc": "<hr><b>Static address only</b>"
            },
            {
                "type": "textfield",
                "subitems": [
                    {
                        "key": "wizard_wifi_address",
                        "desc": "Address, with its mask (192.168.1.50/24)",
                        "defaultValue": "",
                        "validator": {
                            "allowBlank": true,
                            "regex": {
                                "expr": "/^[0-9]{1,3}(\\.[0-9]{1,3}){3}\\/[0-9]{1,2}$/",
                                "errorText": "An address with its mask, as 192.168.1.50/24"
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "key": "wizard_wifi_gateway",
                        "desc": "Gateway",
                        "defaultValue": "",
                        "validator": {
                            "allowBlank": true
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "key": "wizard_wifi_dns",
                        "desc": "DNS servers, separated by spaces",
                        "defaultValue": "",
                        "validator": {
                            "allowBlank": true
                        }
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "type": "multiselect",
                "desc": "<hr>The default route and the DNS servers of the WiFi replace those of the NAS: for a NAS on WiFi alone, not one with a cable.<br><b>Warning:</b> a wrong setting can leave the NAS out of reach of the network. A restart undoes it, unless a boot task connects; otherwise refer to the documentation of your NAS for a reset of its network configuration (on Synology NAS, the RESET button held for about 4 seconds).",
                "subitems": [
                    {
                        "key": "wizard_wifi_default_route",
                        "desc": "Default route through the WiFi",
                        "defaultValue": false
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    }
]
